{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"semidivine-proud-fieldmouse","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nscarlet-unsocial-limpkin (Gerrit 3500, `8469f0a5ede`) added `_may_be_closed` and `_sets_closed` to `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`. Its LLM review left 2 advisory findings:\n- `_sets_closed` calls `.get` on `event[\"data\"]` and `data[\"fields\"]` without checking they are dicts. A raw event whose `data` or `fields` is a non-empty string or list raises `AttributeError`. That happens inside `_scoped_state`'s `except` handler, so `rebar verify-opcert` crashes with a traceback instead of judging the ticket. A crash exits non-zero (so the gate does not pass), but the operator gets a traceback, not a named ticket.\n- No test drives 3 of `_may_be_closed`'s \"may be closed\" branches: an event file that does not parse, JSON that is not an object, and a ticket directory with no active event files.\n\n## Approach\n\nIn `_sets_closed`, treat a non-dict `data` or `fields` as \"may be closed\" (return True), so a malformed event is judged like any other unreadable ticket rather than crashing. Add tests for the 4 cases in `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`, reusing `_write_event` (extended to write raw text) and `_break_show_ticket`.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nWith `show_ticket` raising for an in-progress ticket and `--require-environment` set, each of these makes the gate exit 1 and report `unreadable ticket state` for it: an event file holding invalid JSON; a file holding a JSON list; a ticket directory whose only files are retired (`.json.retired`); a STATUS event whose `data` is a string. The last case raises `AttributeError` against the current code. Then `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A raw event whose `data` or `fields` is not an object no longer crashes `rebar verify-opcert`; the ticket is judged and reported `unreadable ticket state`: shown by a test that fails on `8469f0a5ede`.\n- [ ] Tests cover an unparseable event file, a non-object JSON file and a directory with no active event files, each judged (exit 1 with a required environment).\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`, and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.","id":"6c2e-f2d9-6264-4c55","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"verify-opcert crashes on a malformed raw event in an unreadable ticket"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795276774990935001,"uuid":"48e5cf92-4c30-4d77-8a3d-d317c158baaf"}